# ============================================================================
# Phase 7 Scenario 3 — Buprenorphine treatment expansion
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Intent: more people with OUD start and stay on buprenorphine.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-08-17, twice over. The previous version said to double
# `moud.enroll.*.prob` for "the post-waiver enroll window". Both halves were
# wrong: that path does not exist, and the X-waiver framing is not supported by
# what the policy actually did.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. THE PATH DOES NOT EXIST
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no `moud.enroll` block. titan/params/moud.yml defines start_time,
# init_coverage, init_at_equilibrium, use_reinit, reinit_prob, post_relapse_rr,
# post_overdose_rr, discontinue_per_month, overdose_scale, injection_scale and
# acceptance. `enroll` exists only under haart, in demographics.
#
# The per-step MOUD initiation probability is `moud.reinit_prob`. moud.py's
# `_get_enroll_prob` fallback is unreachable in calibrated runs, because the
# top-level reinit_prob override takes precedence and is always fitted.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. THE X-WAIVER FRAMING IS REFUTED BY THE POLICY'S OWN EVALUATION
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The X-waiver was eliminated on 2023-01-12. Evaluations agree it increased the
# number of prescribers and did NOT increase the number of patients starting
# buprenorphine:
#
#   * +1,938 prescribers as a level change, +595/month as a slope change
#     (Buprenorphine Dispensation After X-Waiver Elimination by Clinician
#     Specialty, Am J Prev Med 2025).
#   * "increases in buprenorphine-prescribing clinicians but no changes in
#     patients initiating buprenorphine" — Chua et al., NEJM 2023,
#     doi:10.1056/NEJMc2312906.
#
# Modelling "post-waiver expansion" as a doubling of patient initiation would
# therefore assert the opposite of the measured effect. If the intent is to model
# the X-waiver specifically, the honest answer is that its effect on initiation
# was null and the scenario is not worth running.
#
# What DOES raise initiation is active linkage at a clinical encounter:
#
#   * D'Onofrio et al., JAMA 2015;313(16):1636-1644 (RCT): 30-day engagement 78%
#     with ED-initiated buprenorphine vs 37% with brief intervention + referral.
#     Ratio 2.11, difference 41 percentage points.
#   * Chambers et al. (observational): aOR 5.86 (95% CI 2.70-12.71).
#
# So a x2 on the initiation rate IS well supported — as a treatment-initiation
# intervention, not as a waiver effect. Reframe the scenario accordingly.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. THE MULTIPLIER IS NOT THE EFFECT SIZE
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Equilibrium MOUD coverage is reinit_prob / (reinit_prob + discontinue_per_month)
# — stated in titan/params/moud.yml and enforced by moud.init_at_equilibrium. So
# doubling the initiation RATE does not double COVERAGE. At trial 561's values:
#
#     baseline  0.11833 / (0.11833 + 0.08847) = 0.572
#     doubled   0.23666 / (0.23666 + 0.08847) = 0.728
#
# +15.6 percentage points, not x2. Report it as a rate change with the coverage
# consequence stated, or the result will read as far weaker than the knob looks.
#
# Note also that raising initiation alone leaves retention untouched. If the
# intervention being modelled includes retention support, moud.discontinue_per_month
# is the second knob and should move in the same arm.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FILL IN — Jun
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   reinit_prob = 2.11 x <fitted moud.reinit_prob>      # after D'Onofrio 78/37
#   Worked at trial 561: 2.11 x 0.11833 = 0.24968
#
# Decide and record: is this arm "treatment initiation doubles" (rate framing,
# above) or "coverage reaches X%" (target framing)? For a coverage target C,
# invert the equilibrium instead:
#
#     reinit_prob = C x discontinue_per_month / (1 - C)
#
# e.g. C = 0.75 at trial 561's discontinue 0.08847 gives reinit_prob = 0.26541.
#
# ============================================================================
